(4346474, 625052, 80904, '<td valign="top">WoW! Love the fisheye effect. Great shot.</td>', 'WoW! Love the fisheye effect. Great shot.', '2007-12-31 00:48:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4346488, 624833, 85886, '<td valign="top">Grats on the ribbon - well deserved.  And thank you for showing how you did it - I was totally perplexed by it and couldn''t work out how that could be done in one shot! :)  Happy New Year to you too</td>', 'Grats on the ribbon - well deserved.  And thank you for showing how you did it - I was totally perplexed by it and couldn''t work out how that could be done in one shot! :)  Happy New Year to you too', '2007-12-31 00:52:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4346502, 625007, 85886, '<td valign="top">I''m blown away that this shot wasn''t placed higher - it''s an absolute gem.</td>', 'I''m blown away that this shot wasn''t placed higher - it''s an absolute gem.', '2007-12-31 00:56:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(4346507, 625094, 83313, '<td valign="top">Looks like this is one I did not get around to voting on. Feedback, as promised:<br/> <br/>Hmmm... (puts on thinking cap):<br/> <br/>I like the idea you put together here. What is that creature? Looks like it may be a metal sculpture.<br/> <br/>I like the composition and the subtle brown shading in the background. The critter attacking Santa is out of focus and hidden in shadows too much, while there is too much brightness on the Santa figure. An additional light on the critter may have helped some. You had a fairly narrow aperture, so my only suggestion for the DOF would have been to back off a little, perhaps using a different lens would have helped it. I suspect the critter is fairly far away and getting it all in focus would have been a trick.<br/> <br/>In a nutshell, I think the DOF and the lighting is what did this one in with the voting.</td>', 'Looks like this is one I did not get around to voting on. Feedback, as promised: Hmmm... (puts on thinking cap): I like the idea you put together here. What is that creature? Looks like it may be a metal sculpture. I like the composition and the subtle brown shading in the background. The critter attacking Santa is out of focus and hidden in shadows too much, while there is too much brightness on the Santa figure. An additional light on the critter may have helped some. You had a fairly narrow aperture, so my only suggestion for the DOF would have been to back off a little, perhaps using a different lens would have helped it. I suspect the critter is fairly far away and getting it all in focus would have been a trick. In a nutshell, I think the DOF and the lighting is what did this one in with the voting.', '2007-12-31 00:57:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4346521, 625013, 60805, '<td valign="top">Deb''s right! just look at your faves. Well Done!<br/> <br/>edited to say i also gave it a 10 :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-12-31 01:03:31.</i></td>', 'Deb''s right! just look at your faves. Well Done! edited to say i also gave it a 10 :)', '2007-12-31 01:02:45.000000', '2007-12-31 01:03:31.000000', 0),
