(4347028, 625094, 82749, '<td valign="top">As promised, some comments:<br/>--Agree with <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=83313" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">yospiff</a> and <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=79955" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">andrewt</a> about lighting and DOF issues, so won''t repeat those comments.  Also agree that composition with regards to placement of Santa and the creature is OK.<br/>--Additional thoughts about DOF: It is very difficult to get good DOF with very small objects, and good DOF is critical for this one.  In addition, using an aperture in the 30''s (or at least upper 20''s) rather than 7.1 would have helped some.  Most of the higher ranked entries in this challenge required and achieved good DOF, and did this by photographing large things.  <br/>--IMHO, I don''t see enough of a connection between Santa and the creature.  Had you picked something more closely connected to Santa or Christmas to attack him (a UPS delivery truck running him over is the first thing that comes to mind), you would have had a better "story" so to speak.  But <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=83313" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">yospiff</a> thought the idea was OK, so I may be wrong here.<br/>--Hope this helps.</td>', 'As promised, some comments:--Agree with  yospiff and  andrewt about lighting and DOF issues, so won''t repeat those comments.  Also agree that composition with regards to placement of Santa and the creature is OK.--Additional thoughts about DOF: It is very difficult to get good DOF with very small objects, and good DOF is critical for this one.  In addition, using an aperture in the 30''s (or at least upper 20''s) rather than 7.1 would have helped some.  Most of the higher ranked entries in this challenge required and achieved good DOF, and did this by photographing large things.  --IMHO, I don''t see enough of a connection between Santa and the creature.  Had you picked something more closely connected to Santa or Christmas to attack him (a UPS delivery truck running him over is the first thing that comes to mind), you would have had a better "story" so to speak.  But  yospiff thought the idea was OK, so I may be wrong here.--Hope this helps.', '2007-12-31 07:30:34.000000', NULL, 0),
