(4355867, 625091, 42100, '<td valign="top">This definitely had something to say...more so than any other entry in this challenge.  I guess nobody wanted to stop and listen.</td>', 'This definitely had something to say...more so than any other entry in this challenge.  I guess nobody wanted to stop and listen.', '2008-01-02 23:22:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4355881, 625091, 66494, '<td valign="top">Hi, you got an 8 from me. And I also believe that it was seriously underrated. Might be that it spoke to me personally a bit too. But I really like your eye.</td>', 'Hi, you got an 8 from me. And I also believe that it was seriously underrated. Might be that it spoke to me personally a bit too. But I really like your eye.', '2008-01-02 23:25:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4356207, 624904, 68504, '<td valign="top">Very winter.  Like a good woodcut.</td>', 'Very winter.  Like a good woodcut.', '2008-01-03 01:21:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4356570, 623549, 77192, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by SoulMan1978:</b></div><hr/><i> Random guess.....Melbourne? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Wow, that was a good guess! Should have guessed it''d be you too, hotpasta. Congratulations on another high finish!<br/> <br/>EDIT: Just noticed that bit about the shutter speed and the hand held! Wow that''s impressive!!!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-01-03 07:30:34.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by SoulMan1978: Random guess.....Melbourne?   Wow, that was a good guess! Should have guessed it''d be you too, hotpasta. Congratulations on another high finish! EDIT: Just noticed that bit about the shutter speed and the hand held! Wow that''s impressive!!!', '2008-01-03 07:28:53.000000', '2008-01-03 07:30:34.000000', 0),
(4356732, 624301, 68256, '<td valign="top">Wow Antonis I''m just now getting back in the flow and seeing this shot....wonderfully composed!  Everything about this is great.  Congrats on the Honorable Mention.</td>', 'Wow Antonis I''m just now getting back in the flow and seeing this shot....wonderfully composed!  Everything about this is great.  Congrats on the Honorable Mention.', '2008-01-03 09:03:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(4356838, 624885, 32767, '<td valign="top">Donsetsfire</td>', 'Donsetsfire', '2008-01-03 09:26:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4356898, 624885, 51538, '<td valign="top">It''s a bit of an adult angle on the world.  Snap down.  The view really is the child''s view and hard as it might have been the view from the lens might have been a bit more of that child''s view up the road to the unknown future of no health insurance, poor education, Democrats that act like Republicans and Republicans that act like Democrats.  In other words, a knee bend for the shot might have brought the personal side of the child more into the composition.  Cynical as usual.  Happy New Year.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-01-03 09:44:41.</i></td>', 'It''s a bit of an adult angle on the world.  Snap down.  The view really is the child''s view and hard as it might have been the view from the lens might have been a bit more of that child''s view up the road to the unknown future of no health insurance, poor education, Democrats that act like Republicans and Republicans that act like Democrats.  In other words, a knee bend for the shot might have brought the personal side of the child more into the composition.  Cynical as usual.  Happy New Year.', '2008-01-03 09:43:31.000000', '2008-01-03 09:44:41.000000', 0),
(4356977, 624969, 53548, '<td valign="top">great empty landscape</td>', 'great empty landscape', '2008-01-03 10:09:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4356980, 624885, 53548, '<td valign="top">good eye. is that a cyclist?</td>', 'good eye. is that a cyclist?', '2008-01-03 10:10:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4356983, 625095, 53548, '<td valign="top">o*h m*y :-)</td>', 'o*h m*y :-)', '2008-01-03 10:10:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4357417, 625030, 23484, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot Kelli. Very well composed and the color tone works very well with this image.</td>', 'Beautiful shot Kelli. Very well composed and the color tone works very well with this image.', '2008-01-03 12:53:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4357446, 624119, 23484, '<td valign="top">I love train track shots. I shoot a lot of them myself. You did an excellent job with the lighting and I think the crop is just fine.</td>', 'I love train track shots. I shoot a lot of them myself. You did an excellent job with the lighting and I think the crop is just fine.', '2008-01-03 13:04:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4357558, 624904, 57229, '<td valign="top">Last couple of weeks in December I kept seeing this low winter sun on trees lightly frosted with snow (or frost), but never had the camera handy. <br/> <br/>Once I had some free time the sun went in for the duration, natch.<br/> <br/>Then one day there it was doing its thing, so I mounted and expedition - tripod, camera, clothes, tram to station, train up the hill...<br/> <br/>But no, when I got to the train station the sun had clocked off again. Last day of challenge so I nipped into the local park and took a fair series of shots...<br/> <br/>This was the first one.</td>', 'Last couple of weeks in December I kept seeing this low winter sun on trees lightly frosted with snow (or frost), but never had the camera handy.  Once I had some free time the sun went in for the duration, natch. Then one day there it was doing its thing, so I mounted and expedition - tripod, camera, clothes, tram to station, train up the hill... But no, when I got to the train station the sun had clocked off again. Last day of challenge so I nipped into the local park and took a fair series of shots... This was the first one.', '2008-01-03 13:54:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4357960, 625029, 11769, '<td valign="top">:) I love how you always make me smile.</td>', ':) I love how you always make me smile.', '2008-01-03 16:02:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4359870, 624119, 40797, '<td valign="top">Way to go sister, This is brilliant!!! Wonderful perspective!!!I love the leading line of the train track and beautiful lighting. That was very nice of your friend to pose for you at the end of the bridge- He made your image for you.  LOVE It! Straight to my favorite folder it goes.</td>', 'Way to go sister, This is brilliant!!! Wonderful perspective!!!I love the leading line of the train track and beautiful lighting. That was very nice of your friend to pose for you at the end of the bridge- He made your image for you.  LOVE It! Straight to my favorite folder it goes.', '2008-01-04 09:20:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4362308, 624885, 32997, '<td valign="top">nice processing dude...I like this one...<br/>wait a minute, I just read the comments...<img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=30982" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Melethia</a> has some explaining to do...<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-01-05 00:48:44.</i></td>', 'nice processing dude...I like this one...wait a minute, I just read the comments... Melethia has some explaining to do...', '2008-01-05 00:46:48.000000', '2008-01-05 00:48:44.000000', 0),
(4365075, 624885, 68504, '<td valign="top">In the zone.</td>', 'In the zone.', '2008-01-06 01:34:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4365667, 624833, 28719, '<td valign="top">Great picture Andrew. Help me to understand how you did this without getting a reflection of the camera.  I''m just getting started with photography and I need to learn all I can.</td>', 'Great picture Andrew. Help me to understand how you did this without getting a reflection of the camera.  I''m just getting started with photography and I need to learn all I can.', '2008-01-06 10:46:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4368362, 623487, 70675, '<td valign="top">very cool picture</td>', 'very cool picture', '2008-01-07 01:04:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4369617, 624904, 30861, '<td valign="top">I think this is basically lovely, but there are some things about it that keep it from rising to the top aesthetic plateau. In no particular order, they are:<br/> <br/>1. The awkward crop of the leftmost trunk where it goes in and out of the frame.<br/> <br/>2. The unfortunate prominence of the lamp post.<br/> <br/>3. The way the people are all clumped in the mid-distance. If the nearest figure were 20 feet closer to us it would work better for me.<br/> <br/>4. The chromatic fringing on the branches. I''m not sure why you didn''t just desat this and get rid of that.<br/> <br/>Still and all, a very evocative image.</td>', 'I think this is basically lovely, but there are some things about it that keep it from rising to the top aesthetic plateau. In no particular order, they are: 1. The awkward crop of the leftmost trunk where it goes in and out of the frame. 2. The unfortunate prominence of the lamp post. 3. The way the people are all clumped in the mid-distance. If the nearest figure were 20 feet closer to us it would work better for me. 4. The chromatic fringing on the branches. I''m not sure why you didn''t just desat this and get rid of that. Still and all, a very evocative image.', '2008-01-07 11:40:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4369637, 624354, 30861, '<td valign="top">I love this one for the title (how could I not?) but as an image it doesn''t engage me at all. Since this is advanced editing, some shadow/highlight work or tone mapping could have accomplished wonders in bringing up the fence to the prominence it deserves. As it is submitted, the bear is not carrying the metaphorical weight he ought to be. I also think it''s cropped just too danged tight on the right, really squeezing that figure into oblivion.</td>', 'I love this one for the title (how could I not?) but as an image it doesn''t engage me at all. Since this is advanced editing, some shadow/highlight work or tone mapping could have accomplished wonders in bringing up the fence to the prominence it deserves. As it is submitted, the bear is not carrying the metaphorical weight he ought to be. I also think it''s cropped just too danged tight on the right, really squeezing that figure into oblivion.', '2008-01-07 11:47:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4369644, 624732, 30861, '<td valign="top">This was one of my higher scores int he challenge actually. I think it''s a fine image. I''m not surprised it finished low, because it''s not really addressing the "perspective" issue in a way people can comprehend. They will see the receding diagonal of the train as the "perspective" part, and that''s not what the picture is about. But very nice PP work and an "arresting" image (pun intended).</td>', 'This was one of my higher scores int he challenge actually. I think it''s a fine image. I''m not surprised it finished low, because it''s not really addressing the "perspective" issue in a way people can comprehend. They will see the receding diagonal of the train as the "perspective" part, and that''s not what the picture is about. But very nice PP work and an "arresting" image (pun intended).', '2008-01-07 11:49:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4369663, 624885, 30861, '<td valign="top">I like this very much, the brooding, metaphorical essence of it. I like the processing, it works very well. What I''m not *sure* I like as much is the "looking down" perspective on the child. I mean, compositionally this works extremely well, and I suppose the metaphor on "child observed" rather than "from the perspective of a child", but still a part of me wants to see you working from a much lower angle here.</td>', 'I like this very much, the brooding, metaphorical essence of it. I like the processing, it works very well. What I''m not *sure* I like as much is the "looking down" perspective on the child. I mean, compositionally this works extremely well, and I suppose the metaphor on "child observed" rather than "from the perspective of a child", but still a part of me wants to see you working from a much lower angle here.', '2008-01-07 11:53:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4369669, 625123, 30861, '<td valign="top">This one works very well for me. It has a strong kinship to Posthumous''s image. The noise is a definite plus IMO. Overall, it''s eerie and horror-movieish, which is a compliment coming from me. I love B-movies :-)</td>', 'This one works very well for me. It has a strong kinship to Posthumous''s image. The noise is a definite plus IMO. Overall, it''s eerie and horror-movieish, which is a compliment coming from me. I love B-movies :-)', '2008-01-07 11:55:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4369729, 624799, 30861, '<td valign="top">As an image, this has much to commend it. The detail is fantastic. As far as meeting the challenge, this really doesn''t answer well to "perspective", and from your comment I can see you know that. Particularly "off" is the title itself, as of course a birds-eye view is conventionally looking down from a great height.<br/> <br/>The image itself can be improved with some shadow recovery and some edge burning to alleviate the very flat sky. Something like this is what I am talking about:<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=630067" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30861/120/630067.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30861/120/630067.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30861/120/630067.jpg"/></a></td>', 'As an image, this has much to commend it. The detail is fantastic. As far as meeting the challenge, this really doesn''t answer well to "perspective", and from your comment I can see you know that. Particularly "off" is the title itself, as of course a birds-eye view is conventionally looking down from a great height. The image itself can be improved with some shadow recovery and some edge burning to alleviate the very flat sky. Something like this is what I am talking about: ', '2008-01-07 12:10:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4369758, 624894, 30861, '<td valign="top">The tonalities on the right half of this image are fantastic. To my eye there''s too much of the very flat-lit wall on the left; it is the least interesting part of the image and it is almost dominant. I also think it would work better if you had set it up so the converging verticals were symmetrical; lining up the right edge vertically has leaned everything else over badly to the right and it''s an unnatural way of seeing. On the other hand, this IS the perspective challenge, so perhaps the unnatural perspective was your goal?</td>', 'The tonalities on the right half of this image are fantastic. To my eye there''s too much of the very flat-lit wall on the left; it is the least interesting part of the image and it is almost dominant. I also think it would work better if you had set it up so the converging verticals were symmetrical; lining up the right edge vertically has leaned everything else over badly to the right and it''s an unnatural way of seeing. On the other hand, this IS the perspective challenge, so perhaps the unnatural perspective was your goal?', '2008-01-07 12:14:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4369783, 625114, 30861, '<td valign="top">Let''s not even try to discuss whether this is a valid take on "perspective", and just deal with the image :-) It''s an endearing shot on an emotional level. The way the "antlers" match the fur is quite amusing. I wish the santa hat were not hiding behind the antlers; I''d have tried to fix that. The BG furniture is very distracting, especially the wooden leg, so you might have tried to find a better place to set up the pose. On the other hand, maybe the dog''s not cooperative? What do I know? Anyway, I got a chuckle from this one :-)</td>', 'Let''s not even try to discuss whether this is a valid take on "perspective", and just deal with the image :-) It''s an endearing shot on an emotional level. The way the "antlers" match the fur is quite amusing. I wish the santa hat were not hiding behind the antlers; I''d have tried to fix that. The BG furniture is very distracting, especially the wooden leg, so you might have tried to find a better place to set up the pose. On the other hand, maybe the dog''s not cooperative? What do I know? Anyway, I got a chuckle from this one :-)', '2008-01-07 12:18:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4369798, 625104, 30861, '<td valign="top">I''m having a hard time relating to this image, largely because it has been "smoothed" to the point of oblivion. Notice in particular how there''s no trace of detail on the back of the glove, which is too bad because that''s the dominant metaphor of the image, what the hand''s doing. On the plus side, this is an excellent use of DOF; you have that right on.</td>', 'I''m having a hard time relating to this image, largely because it has been "smoothed" to the point of oblivion. Notice in particular how there''s no trace of detail on the back of the glove, which is too bad because that''s the dominant metaphor of the image, what the hand''s doing. On the plus side, this is an excellent use of DOF; you have that right on.', '2008-01-07 12:20:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4369809, 624969, 30861, '<td valign="top">This image is deceptively powerful. It is quiet and subdued tot he point of being almost matter-of-fact, yet something in it is singing. I imagine it is even more wonderful when seen at a larger size, when the dusting of snow on the trees has a chance to assert itself in counterpoint to the almost total lack of detail elsewhere. It''s not every day a totally blown out sky actually works, but it sure does here :-)</td>', 'This image is deceptively powerful. It is quiet and subdued tot he point of being almost matter-of-fact, yet something in it is singing. I imagine it is even more wonderful when seen at a larger size, when the dusting of snow on the trees has a chance to assert itself in counterpoint to the almost total lack of detail elsewhere. It''s not every day a totally blown out sky actually works, but it sure does here :-)', '2008-01-07 12:23:23.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(4369817, 625095, 30861, '<td valign="top">This is outstanding. It was one of my high scores given. The only nit I have (and it isn''t much of a one) is that the reflection portion seems a little muddy, and I wonder if you can crisp that part up simply by selecting the top half of the image and running some curves on it. Lovely shot, and deserving of a better score than it received IMO.</td>', 'This is outstanding. It was one of my high scores given. The only nit I have (and it isn''t much of a one) is that the reflection portion seems a little muddy, and I wonder if you can crisp that part up simply by selecting the top half of the image and running some curves on it. Lovely shot, and deserving of a better score than it received IMO.', '2008-01-07 12:25:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4369826, 625030, 30861, '<td valign="top">The color toning here is exceptional. The overall effect of the image is quite nice. The whole danged thing is leaning over to the right, though; I wish you''d rotated CCW to correct that. I also wish you''d pulled a little more shadow detail up. Still, a lovely shot.</td>', 'The color toning here is exceptional. The overall effect of the image is quite nice. The whole danged thing is leaning over to the right, though; I wish you''d rotated CCW to correct that. I also wish you''d pulled a little more shadow detail up. Still, a lovely shot.', '2008-01-07 12:27:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4369845, 625115, 30861, '<td valign="top">This is my kinda shot :-) I like it very much. It''s only marginally connected tot he challenge topic, which explains its relatively low score vis a vis the quality. For me the bird is a little too centered; I think you have excess area on the left you can whack off to pull the bird over closer to the left edge. I realize you have him right smack on the 1/3 line, but in my experience the 1/3 lines are too far into the image when you do stretched formats; I tend to work closer to a rule of fourths on skinny shots. That''s just my opinion though. Nice work!</td>', 'This is my kinda shot :-) I like it very much. It''s only marginally connected tot he challenge topic, which explains its relatively low score vis a vis the quality. For me the bird is a little too centered; I think you have excess area on the left you can whack off to pull the bird over closer to the left edge. I realize you have him right smack on the 1/3 line, but in my experience the 1/3 lines are too far into the image when you do stretched formats; I tend to work closer to a rule of fourths on skinny shots. That''s just my opinion though. Nice work!', '2008-01-07 12:32:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4369855, 625121, 30861, '<td valign="top">This one''s outstanding. Love the "risking life and limb" component of it. Certainly nails the challenge theme in a fairly off the wall way. I''m surprised it didn''t finish a bit higher. I really have no nits here. Good work.</td>', 'This one''s outstanding. Love the "risking life and limb" component of it. Certainly nails the challenge theme in a fairly off the wall way. I''m surprised it didn''t finish a bit higher. I really have no nits here. Good work.', '2008-01-07 12:34:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4369881, 624751, 30861, '<td valign="top">Conceptually this is very nice, if a bit off the beaten path for a "perspective" challenge. The cropping on the bottom and right is simply excellent. The processing, unfortunately, is a whole other story. It''s got an overall muddy, green tint to it that is damaging you. I see you are using lightroom, which is an excellent color management tool, so it makes me wonder if the color is set right on your monitor. Aside from color and noise issues, this is a very nice image.</td>', 'Conceptually this is very nice, if a bit off the beaten path for a "perspective" challenge. The cropping on the bottom and right is simply excellent. The processing, unfortunately, is a whole other story. It''s got an overall muddy, green tint to it that is damaging you. I see you are using lightroom, which is an excellent color management tool, so it makes me wonder if the color is set right on your monitor. Aside from color and noise issues, this is a very nice image.', '2008-01-07 12:40:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4371689, 624716, 67145, '<td valign="top">hey alice .. <br/>brilliant photograph .. such excellent &amp; brilliant colours .. <br/>this might have gone heaps better in the object isolation by contrast challenge .. !! .. lol .. its great example of perspective tho ..  :)</td>', 'hey alice .. brilliant photograph .. such excellent & brilliant colours .. this might have gone heaps better in the object isolation by contrast challenge .. !! .. lol .. its great example of perspective tho ..  :)', '2008-01-07 20:32:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4371946, 624475, 67841, '<td valign="top">Surreal imagery - very cool!</td>', 'Surreal imagery - very cool!', '2008-01-07 21:43:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4372798, 624475, 25355, '<td valign="top">well done for a another high-scoring K10D image ;-)</td>', 'well done for a another high-scoring K10D image ;-)', '2008-01-08 01:26:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4375031, 625120, 63267, '<td valign="top">Awesome photo Alfredo.  The exposure/lighting is just spot on and the comp works very well with the image.  The way the jump is not in the image really adds the drama that this challenge was asking for.  I am sorry this didn''t make the fonrt page as it should have, but rest assured it is still one of the best in the challenge.  Congrats on the top 10!</td>', 'Awesome photo Alfredo.  The exposure/lighting is just spot on and the comp works very well with the image.  The way the jump is not in the image really adds the drama that this challenge was asking for.  I am sorry this didn''t make the fonrt page as it should have, but rest assured it is still one of the best in the challenge.  Congrats on the top 10!', '2008-01-08 18:19:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4379025, 625120, 72316, '<td valign="top">Unbelievable, amazing,......sugoi!!!</td>', 'Unbelievable, amazing,......sugoi!!!', '2008-01-09 19:07:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4379566, 625097, 67697, '<td valign="top">This is interesting.  What message were you trying to convey here? lol.  Actually if you make this just a square crop you''d have a very pretty texture picture.  Nice find!</td>', 'This is interesting.  What message were you trying to convey here? lol.  Actually if you make this just a square crop you''d have a very pretty texture picture.  Nice find!', '2008-01-09 21:55:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(4380428, 625120, 75809, '<td valign="top">i just have to say this is truly a great photo.</td>', 'i just have to say this is truly a great photo.', '2008-01-10 03:52:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4398866, 625013, 69691, '<td valign="top">wow nice work! i like this shot alot. very dramatic image really catches your eye with the fog and the black and white looks really classy.</td>', 'wow nice work! i like this shot alot. very dramatic image really catches your eye with the fog and the black and white looks really classy.', '2008-01-17 00:01:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4403517, 624978, 74663, '<td valign="top">I''ve been there many times!</td>', 'I''ve been there many times!', '2008-01-18 21:03:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4417156, 624119, 29011, '<td valign="top">Welcome back to the challenges :)<br/>This is a splendid shot, Sandy. I really like it in color. Reckon it would also be good for b/w.</td>', 'Welcome back to the challenges :)This is a splendid shot, Sandy. I really like it in color. Reckon it would also be good for b/w.', '2008-01-23 10:01:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4432184, 625078, 89419, '<td valign="top">i like the angle</td>', 'i like the angle', '2008-01-28 10:04:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(4434764, 623487, 60862, '<td valign="top">Hmm.  I''m surprised this didn''t break 6.  I still like it. :)</td>', 'Hmm.  I''m surprised this didn''t break 6.  I still like it. :)', '2008-01-28 20:51:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4443893, 624526, 60862, '<td valign="top">Wow, that''s really cool, Jeb!</td>', 'Wow, that''s really cool, Jeb!', '2008-01-31 15:33:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4459578, 625080, 89875, '<td valign="top">You need to show your pictures!!!! They are amazing!</td>', 'You need to show your pictures!!!! They are amazing!', '2008-02-05 09:07:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4482520, 624475, 31637, '<td valign="top">I have been itching to do a shot like this. Very nice composition. I live around here in Staten Island. One of the roads similar to this is Arden ave. some very Dutch names!.My  problem is all that traffic regardless of the hour. This is how you do it, great exposure considering the low light, textures are nice and the contrast of the trees makes this.</td>', 'I have been itching to do a shot like this. Very nice composition. I live around here in Staten Island. One of the roads similar to this is Arden ave. some very Dutch names!.My  problem is all that traffic regardless of the hour. This is how you do it, great exposure considering the low light, textures are nice and the contrast of the trees makes this.', '2008-02-13 04:33:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(4492791, 624301, 64670, '<td valign="top">Wonderful image.</td>', 'Wonderful image.', '2008-02-17 16:12:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4531745, 624119, 57775, '<td valign="top">Great leading lines here!  I love the figure framed by the tunnel.</td>', 'Great leading lines here!  I love the figure framed by the tunnel.', '2008-03-01 23:53:22.000000', NULL, 0),
